            <ArticleTitle>Autoimmune Thyroiditis Presenting as Psychosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>174-176</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11919/j.issn.1002-0829.216059</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hashimoto's thyroiditis is a rare condition associated mainly with neurological symptoms. It contains an abundant amount of auto-antibodies in the blood. Only a few cases of behavioral symptoms without significant neurological disturbances have been recorded in the literature. In this view, our case is unique as it was not associated with overt hypothyroid manifestations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
